// sandbox.proto: the API between sandboxctl (or any other client) and
// sandboxd, the daemon that restores, runs and destroys microVMs.
//
// The daemon is the server and listens on a Unix socket: rootless mode
// uses $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sandboxd/sandboxd.sock, jailer mode
// /run/sandboxd/sandboxd.sock (ADR-0006). Who may connect is decided by
// the socket's file permissions; the daemon records the caller's UID with
// every run.
//
// One Run is one command in one fresh clone of a base snapshot. The clone
// is destroyed afterwards, whatever happens, and one audit record is
// written for it. docs/learn/11-the-daemon-and-a-run.md explains the life
// of a run.

